From 9c259cc252f5f80c1463d5c29368548ae765f48e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FileZilla dark mode port <fzdark@localhost>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 14:51:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] build: accept wxWidgets 3.3 in configure.ac

configure.ac refused wxWidgets 3.3 outright:

    if test "${WX_VERSION_MAJOR}.${WX_VERSION_MINOR}" = "3.3"; then
      AC_MSG_ERROR([You must use wxWidgets 3.2.x, ...])

wxWidgets 3.3 is a stable series, not a development snapshot, and FileZilla
needs it: 3.3 is the first release whose wxMessageBox is dark-mode aware,
which the dark mode work depends on. Downgrade the check to a warning so any
version other than 3.2 is at least reported rather than rejected.

Only configure.ac is touched. The generated configure is not part of the
series: C:\fzdark\scripts\build-filezilla.sh runs autoreconf before configure,
so the generated copy is always rebuilt from this source.
---
 configure.ac | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index 5b1c1c1..43350c7 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -226,8 +226,10 @@ if test "$buildmain" = "yes"; then
         equivalent variable and wxWidgets version is $MIN_WX_VERSION or above.
       ])
     fi
-    if test "${WX_VERSION_MAJOR}.${WX_VERSION_MINOR}" = "3.3"; then
-      AC_MSG_ERROR([You must use wxWidgets 3.2.x, development versions of wxWidgets are not supported.])
+    # wxWidgets 3.3 is a stable release and FileZilla needs it for the dark mode
+    # aware wxMessageBox (3.3.3). Warn instead of refusing to build.
+    if test "${WX_VERSION_MAJOR}.${WX_VERSION_MINOR}" != "3.2"; then
+      AC_MSG_WARN([Building against wxWidgets ${WX_VERSION_MAJOR}.${WX_VERSION_MINOR}. FileZilla 3.71.1 was released against the wxWidgets 3.2 series.])
     fi
 
     # --universal=no doesn't work correctly, it still accepts universal builds. Reject it manually here.
-- 
